Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:16:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] video_core: reinterpret RG8 colour as D16 depth in OpenGL
 (Build 148)

The other direction of Build 147: DEAD OR ALIVE Dimensions also writes RG8 data
back into its 16-bit depth buffer (log: 'Unimplemented reinterpretation
RG8(0x8058) -> D16(0x81a5)'). New shader rg8_to_d16.frag writes gl_FragDepth
(R = high byte, G = low byte, as in 3DS memory) into the depth texture attached
to the blit framebuffer, depth test always/writes on, colour writes off.
Shaders checked with glslangValidator as GLSL 4.30 and GLSL ES 3.10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
